<mxCell id="rel536" value="company_id (SET NULL)" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;fontSize=10;html=1;rounded=0;startArrow=ERZeroToOne;endArrow=ERZeroToMany;startFill=0;endFill=0;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=6;strokeColor=#4d4d4d;" edge="1" parent="1" source="tbl75" target="tbl117"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="rel537" value="api_key_id (SET NULL)" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;fontSize=10;html=1;rounded=0;startArrow=ERZeroToOne;endArrow=ERZeroToMany;startFill=0;endFill=0;jumpStyle=arc;jumpSize=6;strokeColor=#4d4d4d;" edge="1" parent="1" source="tbl96" target="tbl117"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note538" value="&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;Schema-wide notes&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• Primary keys are surrogate &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;BIGSERIAL&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; columns.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;parcel_number&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; values are drawn from the sequence &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;parcel_number_seq&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; (V45); PTO numbers are generated by &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;PTONumberGeneratorImpl&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;parcels&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; and &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;parcel_boundaries&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; carry a &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;version&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; column used as a JPA &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;@Version&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; optimistic-lock / offline-sync token.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;pto_records&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; uses soft delete (&amp;lt;i&amp;gt;deleted_at&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;deleted_by&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;) — rows are never physically removed.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• The framework-managed Flyway table &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;flyway_schema_history&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; is omitted." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=16;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="50" y="2150" width="680" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note539" value="&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;Bidirectional parcel ↔ PTO link&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;The schema contains &amp;lt;b&amp;gt;two&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt; independent foreign keys:&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;pto_records.parcel_id → parcels.id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; (V20)&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;parcels.pto_id → pto_records.id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; (V12)&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;Both are maintained in code: &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;PTOServiceImpl.approvePTO()&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; sets the parcel to ALLOCATED and points &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;parcel.pto&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; at the approved PTO, while &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;revokePTO()&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; resets the parcel to AVAILABLE and clears &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;pto_id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;. Both links are modelled because both exist in the database." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=16;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="760" y="2150" width="680" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note540" value="&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;Polymorphic / unconstrained references&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;documents.related_entity_type&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; + &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;related_entity_id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; reference PTO, PARCEL, RESIDENT, HOUSEHOLD or BUSINESS (no physical FK).&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;notifications.entity_type&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; + &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;entity_id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; (no physical FK).&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;audit_logs.entity_type&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; + &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;entity_id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; are polymorphic and &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;performed_by&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; stores a username, so no FK exists.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;residents.business_id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; (V39) and &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;business_occupancies.household_id&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; (V38) were added without a FOREIGN KEY constraint — shown as dashed logical relationships." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=16;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1470" y="2150" width="680" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note541" value="&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;Tables without (complete) application support&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;report_schedules&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; is created by migration V17, which explicitly labels it a “future enhancement”. No JPA entity, repository, service or controller exists — it is a schema-only artefact.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;gis_layers&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; has an entity (&amp;lt;i&amp;gt;GisLayer&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;) and repository, but no service/controller write path; the GIS page reads parcel geometry rather than layers.&amp;lt;br&amp;gt;• &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;households&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt;, &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;residents&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; and &amp;lt;i&amp;gt;business_occupancies&amp;lt;/i&amp;gt; have entities and repositories but no service/controller, so they can currently only be populated by direct data operations." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=16;fillColor=#fff9c4;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2180" y="2150" width="760" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root>
</mxGraphModel>
</diagram>
</mxfile>
